1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,760
The AI says, "It's done."

2
00:00:01,809 --> 00:00:02,206
Great.

3
00:00:02,319 --> 00:00:08,760
But I'm still clicking through the app, taking screenshots, and explaining what went wrong.

4
00:00:08,830 --> 00:00:10,483
That's why I built Ming.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,419
Let's try it with Shipboard, a small task app.

6
00:00:17,851 --> 00:00:20,291
I've left a bug in this version.

7
00:00:20,489 --> 00:00:24,951
I upload the HTML file, and there's my app, ready to check.

8
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:36,568
Here's what I need: reject an empty task, add a new one, and keep it after a refresh.

9
00:00:36,851 --> 00:00:40,547
I just write those requirements in plain English.

10
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:49,568
Now I ask Seed two point zero Pro for a checklist.

11
00:00:49,979 --> 00:00:56,270
It reads my requirements and the page, then suggests what to do and what should happen.

12
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:05,845
I can review the steps before anything runs.

13
00:01:06,021 --> 00:01:09,335
Once they look right, I click Approve and check.

14
00:01:09,340 --> 00:01:12,483
Ming carries out those actions in the browser.

15
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:20,887
There it is.

16
00:01:21,064 --> 00:01:24,866
The task was added, but it's gone after the refresh.

17
00:01:25,319 --> 00:01:31,228
Ming caught the failure, and saved what actually happened so I can inspect it.

18
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:39,206
Now I copy these instructions for my coding AI.

19
00:01:39,574 --> 00:01:43,015
They include the steps and what went wrong.

20
00:01:43,468 --> 00:01:47,334
Copying doesn't fix the code or contact an assistant.

21
00:01:47,745 --> 00:01:50,334
I pass the brief over separately.

22
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:58,398
For this demo, I've prepared a corrected version.

23
00:01:58,660 --> 00:02:02,377
I upload it and run the same checklist again.

24
00:02:02,511 --> 00:02:05,611
This time, the task stays after the refresh.

25
00:02:05,915 --> 00:02:09,185
Both results are kept, so I can compare them.

26
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:23,655
IBM Bob helped build the original browser runner, evidence history, model adapter, and repair

27
00:02:23,660 --> 00:02:24,440
foundations.

28
00:02:24,894 --> 00:02:27,760
Here is an original task summary.

29
00:02:28,064 --> 00:02:35,291
After my trial quota ran out, I used other development tools to finish and refine the product.

30
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:41,143
Of course, passing these checks doesn't mean everything is perfect.

31
00:02:41,383 --> 00:02:48,526
But now, I can give my coding AI clear evidence of what works and what needs fixing.

32
00:02:48,723 --> 00:02:49,653
That's Ming.
